| Evidence item | Required before PHI processing | Current status | Evidence location | Owner | Notes |
|---|---:|---|---|---|---|
| Signed Business Associate Agreement (BAA) | Yes | Pending | TBD | Clinic compliance owner | Must be fully executed before any scheduling PHI is entered into the SaaS. |
| HIPAA security documentation | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / clinic compliance owner | Must describe administrative, technical, and physical safeguards for scheduling PHI. |
| Third-party security assessment evidence | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / security reviewer | SOC 2 Type II, HITRUST, penetration test attestation, or equivalent current evidence is acceptable if approved by the clinic. |
| CVE management process evidence | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / security reviewer | Must show intake, severity classification, remediation expectations, and customer notification practices. |
| SBOM or equivalent component inventory | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / security reviewer | Must cover in-scope hosted services or provide an equivalent inventory acceptable to the clinic. |
| Encryption and access control evidence | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / security reviewer | Must support encryption in transit and at rest, individual accounts, MFA, RBAC, and auditable access. |
| Audit and operational reporting evidence | Yes | Pending | TBD | SaaS vendor / clinic technical owner | Must include access events, scheduling changes, configuration changes, sync failures, and reminder failures where supported. |
